# Dispatch kernel

**Invariant:** `lean_context ⇒ dispatch(heavy read | author | implement) off-seat; lead orchestrates`.
Before non-trivial implement or breadth investigation ask "can this be a dispatch?" — default **yes**;
stay in-seat only for trivial/local touches or latency-sensitive tight-loop debugging.

## Read side — Explore-first

`loci_unknown ∨ ≥3_files ∨ 2nd_speculative_grep ⇒ Task(subagent_type="explore")` (parallel when ≥2
independent questions). Explore ≡ Cursor subagent; in-seat Grep/Read is not Explore. Omit `model=`.
Sparse work item (`density_triage` unset or `recon_pending`) ⇒ recon front-half — the conductor's S2 — before any
**implement** dispatch (`require_implement_ready` guards the implement leg, not the conductor spawn; spawning onto
`recon_pending` is the intended path). Exempt: `mechanical`/`trivial`, or a dense spec with `files_expected` +
`acceptance_criteria`. **Todo stage attrs (`density_triage`, `implement_ready`) are a write-once spawn seed; after
spawn the scoreboard fold is current state — never route off the attr while G1–G3 are open.** A bugfix on pattern P
sweeps the service for P before it is complete (`[quality:bug-class-sweep]`).

## Ladder + binder order

| Need | Path | Autonomy |
|---|---|---|
| Mechanical implement | `team_dispatch(op=generate, seat=cursor-sdk)` → Composer (omit `model=`) | autonomous |
| Investigate residual · conductor drive | Composer (omit `model=`, `contract=light-bounded\|investigate`) — returns `OPEN FORK:` lines, never binds | autonomous |
| Greater reasoning / independent check | **`cdp/fable`** width · **`cdp/opus-5`** bind/review — `team_dispatch(model=…)` announce one line `CDP: <trigger> — <why>`, then proceed | autonomous on trigger |
| Premium live checkout | `cursor/claude-opus-5` — inform-then-proceed (wait only if premium spend is paused) | announce |

CDP trigger (any): architecture-suitability live · ≥2 co-primary hypotheses unranked · invariant-touching /
cross-agent bind · recurrence ≥2 · external check needed. Anti-trigger: mechanical · single-subsystem · loci known.

`seat_unsure ⇒ consult(independent_binder)`; `binder_unsure ⇒ human` (rare — true operator-only gates).
Binder order: `cdp/opus-5` (non-Anthropic producer) → **`cdp/fable`** (producer is Opus, or Opus unsure) →
`cursor/gpt-5.6-terra|sol` **only on explicit Other-Models pin**.
`cursor/claude-opus-5` is step 1, not ladder-top. CDP operator seat stuck ⇒ `cursor-auto` → nested
`cursor-sdk` (Composer `contract=light-bounded` limb / `cursor/claude-opus-5` explicit premium), never a Cowork Ask to the human.

## Hard walls

- `anthropic/*` API **PROHIBITED**; `cursor/claude-fable-5{,-1}` blocked (cost, incl. Fable 5.1 launch 2026-09-01 — same headline $/M) — Fable is `cdp/fable` only.
- Non-primary cursor model bind (`Task model=` or `team_dispatch model=cursor/*` not named as workflow-primary
  by a standing rule/skill) ⇒ **operator-gated**: propose slug + why, wait. Named exceptions fire with an announce.
- `judgment_closed ∧ mechanical_remainder ⇒ split`: reasoning model **binds** (`light-bounded`), nested
  `seat=cursor-sdk` **implements** (`implement` | `pure-mechanical`, `nest_under` the live lease holder). The
  conductor obeys this inside its score; on `cursor-auto` the redirect is substrate (`decision:autonomous-dispatch-bounds`).
- Before **any** `team_dispatch` (incl. `role=cursor-implement`): consult-routing gate is binding; second advisor
  on a fork ⇒ name the peer in each packet; `busy_status` shows `agent_bus`+`stargate`+`git_integration_worker` up.
- Same fix failed twice ⇒ stop; consult with the failure context — never a third variant.
- `operator_names(dispatch_param) ∧ ¬admits(param) ⇒ report(failure) ∧ wait` — model, effort/tier, or any other
  explicitly named value that fails to admit gets reported, not silently substituted for a different value while
  proceeding. That substitution **is** fallback logic (standing user rule: prefer no fallback logic; prompt first
  when it matters) — it is not a judgment call this seat gets to make unasked, even for a "just an effort knob"
  substitution (incident: `agent-bus:9638`, Fable Max → High swap, 2026-09-01).

## Front door

```
∀ operator_request:
  explicit override (/path-sim · /layer · root id · belt) ≺ tree
  mutates_durable_state (code · graph · docs · services) ⇒ conductor session, bound to exactly one todo: work item
  else (answer · review · judgment, attended)          ⇒ in-seat, threadless — reasoning-posture + hypothesize-simulate aperture
```

Both B legs (B-arc | B-mech) spawn a T0 conductor; the materializer refuses a non-todo `source_ref` and a
conductor-less `source_ref` ship is rejected. The conductor mints its own thread + sparse score; its CHECKPOINT is a
reconstitution index, never completion authority. Charter-tick enrollment is not a terminal for new work.
`seat=cursor-auto ⇒ silent SOP, ¬ prompt operator for routing/ack`; IDE lead MAY ask ack on material forks,
default recommend-and-proceed. True operator-only ⇒ `status:needs-attended` + one recommended answer.

**Task subagent parity:** mutating Task prompts ⇒ parent injects alwaysApply kernel (`task-subagent-parity_ulg` · `subagent-strategy` § Task subagent parity) — subagents start cold.

